<report>
<line><title>Logrank and Wilcoxon tests</title></line>
<line><block name="outer"></line>
<line><title><in>title</in><in>strata</in>:</title><block name="groups"></line>
<line></line>
<line><u><subtotal>For group <in>grp</in></subtotal></u></line>
<line>Observed deaths = <in>obs</in></line>
<line>Extent of exposure to risk of death = <in>ext</in></line>
<line>Relative rate = <in>rel</in></block></line>
<line></line>
<line>test statistics:</line>
<line><in>rank</in></line>
<line></line>
<line>variance-covariance matrix:<block name="covar"></line>
<line><in>mat</in></block></line>
<line></line>
<line>Chi-square for equivalence of death rates = <in>chi</in>  <pval><in>p</in></pval></line>
<line><block name="trends">Chi-square for trend = <in>trend</in> <pval> <in>p_trend</in></pval></line>
<line></block><block name="strata"></line>
<line><title><in>test</in> for COMBINED STRATA</title><subtotal>:</subtotal></line>
<line></line>
<table>
<tr><th>Stratum</th><th>Deaths</th><th>Extent of exposure to risk of death</th><th>Relative rate</u><block name="stratum"></td></tr>
<tr><td><in>grp</in></td><td><in>res</in></td><td><in>sum</in></td><td><in>tot</in></block></td></tr>
</table>
<line></line>
<line>overall chi-square = <in>chi_strata</in>  <pval><in>p_strata</in></pval><block name="strata_trend"></line>
<line>Chi-square for trend = <in>strata_trend</in><pval>  <in>p_strata_trend</in></pval></line>
<line></block></line>
<line></block><block name="hazards"></line>
<line>Hazard Ratio  <ci>(approximate <in>pc</in>% confidence interval)</ci><block name="hazard"></line>
<line><in>vs</in> = <in>haz</in>  <ci>(<in>from</in> to <in>to</in>)</ci></block></line>
<line><block name="cml"></line>
<line>Conditional maximum likelihood estimates:</line>
<line>Hazard Ratio = <in>hr</in></line>
<line><ci>Exact Fisher <in>pc</in>% confidence interval = <in>llf</in> to <in>ulf</in></ci></line>
<line><pval>Exact Fisher one sided <in>p1f</in>, two sided <in>p2f</in></pval></line>
<line><ci>Exact mid-P <in>pc</in>% confidence interval = <in>llm</in> to <in>ulm</in></ci></line>
<line><pval>Exact mid-P one sided <in>p1m</in>, two sided <in>p2m</in></pval></line>
<line></block></block></block></line>
<line></line>
</report>
